# Feature 195 — paths permitted to call BlueprintPublicationId.Compute / ComputeFromDefinition.
#
# ONE PRODUCER: the Register Service mints a definition's publication id. Everything else reads the
# value it returns. This list may only SHRINK — never add an entry to make a build pass.
#
# Recovery is the one legitimate non-producer: it VERIFIES rather than mints, recomputing the id from
# the bytes it received and comparing to the transaction's own id. That check is what makes the
# identity self-anchoring, so forbidding it would remove the property the feature adds.
#
# THE PRODUCER — the per-register publish endpoint.
src/Services/Sorcha.Register.Service/Program.cs

# THE PRODUCER — the system register is a register, and a blueprint published to it is a definition
# like any other. Same canonical form, same construction, so recovery needs ONE verification rule
# rather than a second one for system blueprints.
src/Services/Sorcha.Register.Service/Services/SystemRegisterService.cs

# VERIFIER, not producer. Recovery recomputes a definition's id from the bytes it received and
# compares to the transaction's own id. Recomputing is the whole point — a node that trusted the id
# it was handed would be verifying nothing.
src/Services/Sorcha.Blueprint.Service/Services/Implementation/BlueprintRecoveryService.cs

# VERIFIER, not producer. The validator's last-resort arm reads a definition straight off the
# register and recomputes its id to check the payload against the transaction that carried it. This
# is an untrusted read; trusting the id it was handed would be verifying nothing.
src/Services/Sorcha.Validator.Service/Services/ValidationEngine.cs
